    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/title"/>
        <IRI>http://www.w3.org/ns/auth/acl</IRI>
        <Literal>Basic Access Control ontology</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>http://www.w3.org/ns/auth/acl</IRI>
        <Literal>Defines the class Authorization and its essential properties,
    and also some classes of access such as read and write. </Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:Access</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Any kind of access to a resource. Don&apos;t use this, use R W and RW</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:Access</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">access</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="acl:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:Access</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">access</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:Append</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Append accesses are specific write access which only add information, and do not remove information.
    For text files, for example, append access allows bytes to be added onto the end of the file.
    For RDF graphs, Append access allows adds triples to the graph but does not remove any.
    Append access is useful for dropbox functionality.
    Dropbox can be used for link notification, which the information added is a notification
    that a some link has been made elsewhere relevant to the given resource.
    </Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:Append</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">append</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:AuthenticatedAgent</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>A class of agents who have been authenticated.
In other words, anyone can access this resource, but not anonymously.
The social expectation is that the authentication process will provide an
identify and a name, or pseudonym.
(A new ID should not be minted for every access: the intent is that the user
is able to continue to use the ID for continues interactions with peers,
and for example to develop a reputation)
</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:AuthenticatedAgent</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Anyone authenticated</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:Authorization</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>An element of access control,
    allowing agent to agents access of some kind to resources or classes of resources</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:Authorization</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>authorization</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:Control</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Allows read/write access to the ACL for the resource(s)</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:Control</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">control</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:Origin</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>An Origin is basically a web site
        (Note WITHOUT the trailing slash after the domain name and port in its URI)
        and is the basis for controlling access to data by web apps
        in the Same Origin Model of web security.
        All scripts from the same origin are given the same right.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:Origin</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Origin</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:seeAlso"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:Origin</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <IRI>https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Origin</IRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:Read</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>The class of read operations</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:Read</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">read</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:Write</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">write</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:accessControl</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>The Access Control file for this information resource.
        This may of course be a virtual resource implemented by the access control system.
        Note also HTTP&apos;s header  Link:  foo.meta ;rel=meta can be used for this.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:accessControl</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>The Access Control file for this information resource.
        This may of course be a virtual resource implemented by the access control system.
        Note that HTTP header `Link: &lt;foo.acl&gt;; rel=&quot;acl&quot;` can also be used for this.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:accessControl</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>access control</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:seeAlso"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:accessControl</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <IRI>https://solidproject.org/TR/wac#acl-link-relation</IRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:accessTo</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>The information resource to which access is being granted.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:accessTo</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>to</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:accessToClass</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>A class of information resources to which access is being granted.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:accessToClass</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>to all in</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:agent</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>A person or social entity to being given the right</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:agent</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>agent</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:agentClass</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>A class of persons or social entities to being given the right</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:agentClass</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>agent class</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:agentGroup</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>A group of persons or social entities to being given the right.
          The right is given to any entity which is a vcard:member of the group,
          as defined by the document received when the Group is dereferenced.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:agentGroup</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>agent group</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:default</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>If a resource has no ACL file (it is 404),
        then access to the resource if given by the ACL of the immediately
        containing directory, or failing that (404) the ACL of the recursively next
        containing directory which has an ACL file.
        Within that ACL file,
        any Authentication which has that directory as its acl:default applies to the
        resource. (The highest directory must have an ACL file.)
</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:default</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>If a resource has no ACL file (it is 404),
        then access to the resource is given by the ACL of the immediately
        containing directory, or failing that (404) the ACL of the recursively next
        containing directory which has an ACL file.
        Within that ACL file,
        any Authorization which has that directory as its acl:default applies to the
        resource. (The highest directory must have an ACL file.)
</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:default</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>default access for things in this</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:defaultForNew</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>THIS IS OBSOLETE AS OF 2017-08-01.   See &apos;default&apos;.
        Was: A directory for which this authorization is used for new files in the directory.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:defaultForNew</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>default access for new things in the object</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:delegates</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Delegates a person or another agent to act on behalf of the agent.
    For example, Alice delegates Bob to act on behalf of Alice for ACL purposes.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:delegates</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">delegates</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:mode</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>A mode of access such as read or write.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:mode</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>access mode</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:origin</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>A web application, identified by its Origin, such as
        &lt;https://scripts.example.com&gt;, being given the right.
        When a user of the web application at a certain origin accesses the server,
        then the browser sets the Origin: header to warn that a possibly untrusted webapp
        is being used.
        Then, BOTH the user AND the origin must have the required access.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:origin</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>origin</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:seeAlso"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:origin</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <IRI>https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Origin</IRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:owner</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>The person or other agent which owns this.
    For example, the owner of a file in a filesystem.
    There is a sense of &quot;right to control&quot;.   Typically defaults to the agent who created
    something, but can be changed.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:owner</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>The person or other agent which owns this.
    For example, the owner of a file in a filesystem.
    There is a sense of right to control.   Typically defaults to the agent who craeted
    something but can be changed.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>acl:owner</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">owner</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#AgentAbility</IRI>
        <Literal>An agent ability that can be recommended by an affordance signifier</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#ContextAuthorizedResource</IRI>
        <Literal>A Resource in a HyperAgents Environment for which Context-Based Access is enabled.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#ContextBasedAccessCondition</IRI>
        <Literal>The top-level SHACL NodeShape which specifies the conditions for accessing a resource in a HyperAgents Environment.

The NodeShape will be a disjunction of conjunctions of NodeShapes, identifying ContextDomain (dynamic), Profiled- or Static- context information available in the HyperAgents Environment, that condition the access.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#ContextBasedAuthorization</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">The Shared Context Authorization base concept identifying the resource for which authorization is given, the type of authorization and the individual / class of individuals to which authorization is given.
Can be further subclassed into access and control (right to alter authorizations) authorizations.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#ContextDomainCondition</IRI>
        <Literal>The SHACL NodeShape that specifies membership in a ContextDomain as a condition for accessing a resource in a Hyperagents Environment.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#ContextDomainGroup</IRI>
        <Literal>A group denoting the dyanmic &quot;membership&quot; in a ContextDomain, that is resources and agents who are determined to satisfy the RSP (RDF Stream Processing) query describing the membership.

The RSP query will involve processing a Stream of dynamic ContextAssertions which define a ContextDimension of a given application (e.g. location), while the ContextDomains are given by the possible role fillers (objects) of the ContextDimension.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#IntentContext</IRI>
        <Literal>The IntentContext is part of the structure of a Signifier and refers to the recommended context for the successful use of a signified affordance.
The IntentContext is given as a list of conditions expressed either as SHACL NodeShape conditions applied to artifact nodes, where the matched-for properties are Literals and the tested conditions include numerical equalities or inequalities, string and substring matches or datetime operations.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#IntentContext</IRI>
        <Literal>Intent Context</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#IntentionDescription</IRI>
        <Literal>The structured language (usually under a JSON form) description of the intention (goal) for which an affordance in exploited, as signalled in a Signifier.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#LLMReasoningAbility</IRI>
        <Literal>The ability of an agent to perform LLM-based reasoning.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#ProfiledContextCondition</IRI>
        <Literal>The SHACL NodeShape that specifies profiled context information as a condition for accessing a resource in a Hyperagents Environment.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#Signifier</IRI>
        <Literal>A Signifier is a modeling element that binds together a Hypermedia MAS resource affordance with the intent of an agent, and the recommended abilities of the agent and the context of the affordance use / invocation.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#StaticContextCondition</IRI>
        <Literal>The SHACL NodeShape that specifies profiled context information as a condition for accessing a resource in a Hyperagents Environment.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#contextGraphURI</IRI>
        <Literal>A property of a Static- or Profiled- ContextCondition SHACL NodeShape identifying the RDF Named Graphs managed in the HyperAgents Environment against which the SHACL shape has to be validated.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#hasAccessCondition</IRI>
        <Literal>Property linking a ContextBasedAuthorization to the ContextBasedAccessCondition (a SHACL NodeShape) that defines the context-based conditions that need to be matched in order to access the resource protected by the ContextBasedAuthorization.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#hasStructuredDescription</IRI>
        <Literal>The property indicating the structured natural language description of a recommended context or the agent intention.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#memberIn</IRI>
        <Literal>Property specifying the membership of an agent identified by a WebID in a ContextDomainGroup.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
